<title>JAPAN: Thai Bangchak tenders to buy crude.</title>
<headline>Thai Bangchak tenders to buy crude.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Bangchak Petroleum Plc has issued a tender to buy 500,000 barrels of Middle East crude oil and 600,000 barrels of Far East crude oil, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes at 6 p.m. (0900 GMT) on Wednesday and offers should be valid until around 6 p.m. on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Middle East crudes are for Oman, Dubai, Murban and other Middle East equivalents, traders said.</p>
<p>Thailand regularly buys 500,000 to one million barrels of Middle East crude oil.</p>
</text>
